- op: discuss  # 636f
  at: '2026-09-09T18:12:13Z'  # 636f
  by: agent  # 636f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 636f
  clock: 3  # 636f
  nonce: 636f  # 636f
  message: "SIZED 2026-09-09. Record and instruments:\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/robit_objc_09092026/ (PLAN.md pre-registered before\nany number existed, runall.sh, RESULT.md).\n\nMY PRE-REGISTERED PREDICTION WAS WRONG AND SO IS THE CLASS ITEM'S STATUS.\nP1 predicted objc would reach FEWER than 10% of its 125 method-kind rows; it\nreaches 21.6% (27/125) across four repos. And INV-linub's ANALYZER STATUS block\nrecords objc as `NOT MEASURED` with a blind-language row of\n`NO EDGE / emit,NOMATCH(method)`. Measured: objc EMITS the call edge, STAMPS\ncall_construct=\"method\", and TYPES HALF ITS EXTERNAL RECEIVERS.\n\nRECEIVER TYPING ON EXTERNAL METHOD CALLS (census, four repos, every calls edge):\n\n    repo            objc calls  in-repo  UNTYPED  typed ext  typed %\n    AFNetworking          1969      297      792        880    52.6%\n    CocoaLumberjack       2581      773      835        973    53.8%\n    fmdb                  1039      148      574        317    35.6%\n    Mantle                 280       53       89        138    60.8%\n    TOTAL                 5869     1271     2290       2308    50.2%\n\nA typed external call carries the class in the module slot\n(objc:NSFileManager:0-0:fileExistsAtPath.:external_symbol) plus a\nreceiver_type_hint and dst_ref.module_path. An untyped one carries the\n`external` sentinel and gate_named_entry refuses it -- correctly, per INV-tapat.\n\nTHE RESIDUAL SHAPE, ISOLATED BY CONTRAST:\n  REACHED     [handle writeData:data]           NSFileHandle *handle\n                                                a LOCAL with a written type\n  UNREACHED   [self.session dataTaskWithRequest:request]\n                                                @property NSURLSession *session\n                                                a PROPERTY reached via self.\nobjc types locals whose type is written, and class-name receivers. It does not\ntype self.<property> receivers. THIS IS A PRECEDENTED SHAPE WITH TWO SIBLING\nFIXES: rust closed it as WI-dizag shape A (self.field, resolve_receiver_type)\nand python worked it in INV-mumov / WI-zamud. Not a new mechanism.\n\nTWO NULL RESULTS THAT ARE CORRECT AND I NEARLY REPORTED AS DEFECTS:\n  * fmdb reaches ZERO db rows. objc's db_read/db_write rows are all Core Data\n    (NSManagedObjectContext, NSPersistentStoreCoordinator); fmdb is a SQLite\n    wrapper over the raw sqlite3_* C API and genuinely does not use Core Data.\n    The catalogue has no sqlite3 rows for objc. An L1 question at most, and not\n    this item's.\n  * AFNetworking's 50 source hits for dataTaskWithRequest are NOT 50 missed\n    sites. 13 of the 15 task-creation edges resolve IN-REPO because AFNetworking\n    defines its own wrapper of the same selector; only 2 reach the external\n    NSURLSession. My source grep counted definitions and calls together.\n\nAN INSTRUMENT ERROR I MADE AND CAUGHT: a first pass reported \"typed slot: 0\" for\nevery repo. That column was arithmetic over two subsets of the SAME bucket\n(external-and-method minus external), so it measured nothing and read as a\ncatastrophic finding. The corrected census is above. This is the fourth time in\ntwo days that a scan reporting the analyzer as broken was the scan being broken.\n\nTHE ITEM'S QUESTION IS ANSWERED: 27/125 = 21.6% R1 rows reached, union over four\nrepos, with CocoaLumberjack's 19 rows across seven boundaries as the positive\ncontrol -- pre-registered because a total zero is also what a NON-RUNNING\nanalyzer produces.\n\nTHE ITEM'S STATED FIRST DELIVERABLE WAS NOT NEEDED. It asked for an objc emitter\nfor measure-catalogue-reach.py; a corpus census answered the question directly,\non real code, which a generated fixture cannot. The emitter is still worth\nhaving for per-row completeness, but it is not on this item's critical path.\n\nSTATUS: done as a SIZING item. The 2,290 untyped external method edges are the\nL3 residual and self.<property> is the named mechanism -- filed separately as\nthe fix item. Sized, not fixed, and deliberately so."  # 636f
